Inference overhead | google/gemma-4-E4B-it
==============================================================================
==============================================================================
1. Generation throughput, watermark on vs off
==============================================================================
 batch  plain tok/s   wm tok/s  overhead
     1         26.9       25.8     4.2%
     4         99.9       87.2    12.7%
    16        398.0      241.4    39.4%
    32        770.4      329.0    57.3%
==============================================================================
2. Cost of watermarking depth (batch size 16)
==============================================================================
 depth   wm tok/s  overhead
     1      392.7     1.3%
     5      369.1     7.3%
    10      337.7    15.2%
    30      241.1    39.4%
Depth is the detection-power / decoding-cost knob: more depth means more
independent g-values per token, and more work per decoding step.
==============================================================================
3. Detection throughput
==============================================================================
cpu        1082.6 texts/s  (0.9 ms per 252-token text)
cuda:0     1241.9 texts/s  (0.8 ms per 252-token text)
Detection is a hash plus a mean: it needs the tokenizer, not the model,
and runs fast enough on CPU that a detection service needs no GPU.
